{"tool_name":"kmdata","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"kmdata","home":"https://github.com/raredd/kmdata","license":"Other","summary":"A curated database of reconstructed individual patient-level data from 153 oncology clinical trials.","addition_date":"2021-11-11T20:53:55.068269Z","last_update_date":"2021-11-11T20:55:57.617954Z","tool_type":["Database portal","Library"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:kmdata","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"steffen@ds.dfci.harvard.edu","name":"Steffen Ventz","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2229-9560","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"ltrippa@ds.dfci.harvard.edu","name":"Lorenzo Trippa","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Robert A Redd"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Database search","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2421"},{"term":"Incident curve plotting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3503"},{"term":"Phasing","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3454"}]}],"name":"KMDATA","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/DATABASE/BAAB037","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2020 The Author(s) 2021. Published by Oxford University Press.We created a database of reconstructed patient-level data from published clinical trials that includes multiple time-to-event outcomes such as overall survival and progression-free survival. Outcomes were extracted from Kaplan-Meier (KM) curves reported in 153 oncology Phase III clinical trial publications identified through a PubMed search of clinical trials in breast, lung, prostate and colorectal cancer, published between 2014 and 2016. For each trial that met our search criteria, we curated study-level information and digitized all reported KM curves with the software Digitizelt. We then used the digitized KM survival curves to estimate (possibly censored) patient-level time-to-event outcomes. Collections of time-to-event datasets from completed trials can be used to support the choice of appropriate trial designs for future clinical studies. Patient-level data allow investigators to tailor clinical trial designs to diseases and classes of treatments. Patient-level data also allow investigators to estimate the operating characteristics (e.g. power and type I error rate) of candidate statistical designs and methods. Database URL: https://10.6084/m9.figshare.14642247.v1","authors":[{"name":"Alexander B.M."},{"name":"Arfe A."},{"name":"Fell G."},{"name":"Louv B."},{"name":"McDunn J."},{"name":"Rahman R."},{"name":"Redd R.A."},{"name":"Trippa L."},{"name":"Vanderbeek A.M."},{"name":"Ventz S."}],"date":"2021-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Database","title":"KMDATA: A curated database of reconstructed individual patient-level data from 153 oncology clinical trials"},"pmcid":"PMC8234134","pmid":"34169314"}],"topic":[{"term":"Data submission, annotation and curation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0219"},{"term":"Oncology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2640"},{"term":"Pathology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0634"},{"term":"Preclinical and clinical studies","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3379"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"KMDATA","home":"https://bio.tools/kmdata","license":"Other","summary":"A curated database of reconstructed individual patient-level data from 153 oncology clinical trials.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:kmdata/db/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":false,"osi"